{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Reunion", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Blast From the Past", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le18ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Past Time Expressions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">three years ago</span> or <span class=\"italic\">last year</span> when you talk about the past.<br><br>  You use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">in 2012</span> when you talk about a year in the past.<br><br>  You use <span class=\"italic\">When I was \u2026 </span> to talk about a period of time.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Expression \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" in \u2026 (month or year)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I went to Paris in 2012.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" last \u2026 (day, month, time, etc.) \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> He ripped the jacket last year.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(number of months or years) \u2026 ago\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I bought this jacket 2 months ago.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Simple Past Tense and Past Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished. <br>  You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that     was happening at a time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.<br>   Regular verbs end in <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"italic\">-ied. </span><br>  Irregular verbs change in different ways.  <br> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did </span> followed by the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask\u2026?   </span><br> <span class=\"italic\">Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"italic\">to do.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For Past Continuous, we add was/were + verb -ing to verbs.<br>   Some verbs need a change to the last letter to add -ing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" do \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"did \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were doing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" carry \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"carried\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" was/were carrying\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" pay \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"paid \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were paying\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" travel \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"traveled \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were traveling\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" rip \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ripped\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" was/were ripped\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" have \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were having\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I did so much shopping when I was traveling in Europe. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They were talking when he ripped his jacket.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "personal shopper", "type": "name"}, {"content": " someone who helps you shop ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I used to get a personal shopper to help me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le18ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about experiences.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "millionaire ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who has more than a million dollars ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Life is tough when you're a millionaire.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le18ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "budget", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an amount of money you can spend at one time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: Peter has budget problems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le18ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to rip", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a long tear or cut in something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter ripped his jacket last year.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le18ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type"